on"r" sets can be checked out from preface section of the [ISA manual]."r" Platform may define and support their own custom instruction sets with"r" ISA prefix X. These sets are highly platform specific and should be"r" detected with their own platform support crates."r" [ISA manual]: https://riscv.org/specifications/ratified/"r" # Platform-specific/agnostic Behavior and Availability"r" Runtime detection depends on the platform-specific feature detection"r" facility and its availability per feature is"r" highly platform/version-specific."r" Still, a best-effort attempt is performed to enable subset/dependent"r" features if a superset feature is enabled regardless of the platform."r#" For instance, if the A extension (`"a"`) is enabled, its subsets (the"#r#" Zalrsc and Zaamo extensions; `"zalrsc"` and `"zaamo"`) are also enabled."#r#" Likewise, if the F extension (`"f"`) is enabled, one of its dependencies"#r#" (the Zicsr extension `"zicsr"`) is also enabled."#r" # Unprivileged Specification"r" The supported ratified RISC-V instruction sets are as follows (OS"r" columns denote runtime feature detection support with or without the"r" minimum supported version):"r" | Literal    | Base    | Linux      |"r" |:---------- |:------- |:---------- |"r#" | `"rv32e"`  | RV32E   | No         |"#r#" | `"rv32i"`  | RV32I   | Yes [^ima] |"#r#" | `"rv64i"`  | RV64I   | Yes [^ima] |"#r" | Literal         | Extension   | Linux               |"r" |:--------------- |:----------- |:------------------- |"r#" | `"a"`           | A           | Yes [^ima]          |"#r#" | `"b"`           | B           | 6.5                 |"#r#" | `"c"`           | C           | Yes                 |"#r#" | `"d"`           | D           | Yes                 |"#r#" | `"f"`           | F           | Yes                 |"#r#" | `"m"`           | M           | Yes [^ima]          |"#r#" | `"q"`           | Q           | No                  |"#r#" | `"v"`           | V           | 6.5                 |"#r#" |